diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the VLAN 5 SVI/bridge on sshswitch (interface br_v5). Mechanism: Campus 2 VLAN 5 hosts can switch locally on switch4, but L3/default-gateway ARP to 10.5.0.254 fails because the gateway interface on sshswitch is down, so frames to/from VLAN 5 never bridge across the uplink toward the router/gateway. Localization: on sshswitch, br_v5 is administratively down while its member subinterfaces exist; “ip -d link show dev br_v5” reports state DOWN, and “ip addr” shows br_v5 state DOWN with 10.5.0.254/24. Its member bond0.5 is present but “bridge_slave state disabled,” consistent with a down bridge. By contrast, the physical trunk to switch4 is healthy: switch4 eth0 and sshswitch eth0 both show UP/LOWER
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=6
