is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the VLAN 5 SVI/bridge on sshswitch (interface br_v5). Mechanism: Campus 2 VLAN 5 hosts can switch locally on switch4, but L3/default-gateway ARP to 10.5.0.254 fails because the gateway interface on sshswitch is down, so frames to/from VLAN 5 never bridge across the uplink toward the router/gateway. Localization: on sshswitch, br_v5 is administratively down while its member subinterfaces exist; “ip -d link show dev br_v5” reports state DOWN, and “ip addr” shows br_v5 state DOWN with 10.5.0.254/24. Its member bond0.5 is present but “bridge_slave state disabled,” consistent with a down bridge. By contrast, the physical trunk to switch4 is healthy: switch4 eth0 and sshswitch eth0 both show UP/LOWER_UP, and switch4’s br_vlan5 is UP with eth0.5 enslaved. Root cause: the VLAN 5 bridge interface (br_v5) on sshswitch is down (misconfiguration/administrative state), not a cabling or trunk link failure. Corrective fix: on sshswitch, bring up br_v5 and ensure its trunk subinterface is forwarding (e.g., ip link set br_v5 up; verify eth0.5 and/or bond0.5 are the intended members and in forwarding state). After br_v5 is up, ARP to 10.5.0.254 from PC1/PC2/DC_PC5 should resolve and inter-VLAN/externals will work without recabling. Recabling the trunk is unnecessary. 
=== END ===